    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Meta is a public company founded in 2004 and headquartered in Menlo Park, CA. Its AI-facing site positions the company as a platform for AI developers, offering access to its models and tools through the Meta Model API, which the site describes as compatible with existing OpenAI SDK clients. The site highlights features including search grounding, which gives models live web access, and support for multi-agent workflows in which a single model can interact with a computer by clicking through applications and moving between interfaces.\n\nMeta's tracked AI product is the Llama family, described as an open-weight model family that is often self-hosted. The site also references several named models and tools: Muse Spark, described as a coding-optimized model; Muse Code, described as a coding agent built to run Muse Spark; and Muse Glimmer, described as a 30-billion-parameter open model optimized for local agent workflows and small enough to run on a Mac or PC with a single consumer GPU. Muse Spark 1.2 is specifically mentioned as the current coding-optimized release.\n\nMeta's SEC filings list it under ticker META with CIK 0001326801, and its most recently recorded annual revenue figure is $200,966,000,000 for the period ending 2025-12-31. The company faces two recorded federal cases in the Northern District of California: Chicken Soup for the Soul, LLC v. Meta Platforms Inc. and Kadrey v. Meta Platforms, Inc.",
